<title>BRAZIL: Bank of Boston Brazil unit nets $50.4 mln in 1996.</title>
<headline>Bank of Boston Brazil unit nets $50.4 mln in 1996.</headline>
<dateline>SAO PAULO 1997-01-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Bank of Boston Corp's Brazil unit Banco de Boston said it reported a net profit of $50.416 million in 1996, down from $52.833 million in the previous year.</p>
<p>The bank's total assets rose to $7.134 billion, up from $4.514 billion in 1995, while its net worth was $358.2 million, against $357.05 million in the previous year, it said in a published financial statement.</p>
<p>Revenues from financial intermediation rose 66.4 percent to $1.146 billion from $689.06 million.</p>
<p>((--Fatima Cristina, Sao Paulo Newsroom 5511 2485412))</p>
